// Plugin: no-chat-trpc-in-surface
// Severity: warn
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Catches:    Any `trpc.chat.<verb>.mutationOptions(...)` reference outside the
//             sanctioned verb-hook home. Inline mutation calls on a chat
//             surface or component bypass the §11 verb-dispatch discipline —
//             the surface ends up owning lifecycle (onSuccess invalidation,
//             error toast, cache plumbing) that should live in one place per
//             verb so the rule for each verb lives in one place.
//
//             Match shape: `trpc.chat.$verb.mutationOptions`. Queries
//             (`queryOptions`, `queryKey`) are NOT touched — surfaces legit
//             read from chat.list / chat.get / chat.messages caches.
//
// Sanctioned homes (per-line suppression):
//   • packages/client/src/features/chat/hooks/use-chat-verbs.ts           (bound verbs)
//   • packages/client/src/features/chat/hooks/use-chat-injection-verbs.ts (injections)
//   • packages/client/src/features/chat/hooks/use-draft-chat-actions.ts   (chat.start)
//   • packages/client/src/features/chat/hooks/use-recent-chats-actions.ts (list verbs)
//
//             Each of those files carries the chat.<verb>.mutationOptions
//             call(s) it owns. Every OTHER file mentioning the pattern is a
//             regression — push the verb into a hook or use an existing one.
//
// Rationale:  docs/architecture/domains/chat.md (chat verb dispatch): "The chat
//             surface NEVER calls trpc.chat.<verb>.
//             mutate directly. … Adding a verb = one function in the bundle
//             hook + one entry in the returned object." Without the lint, a
//             new feature's "let me just inline this one mutation" decision
//             silently breaks the centralization that makes verbs uniform.
//
// Suppress:   // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-chat-trpc-in-surface: <reason>
//             (Used in the sanctioned verb-hook homes listed above; per-line
//             with a path/justification comment.)
//
// Refs:       docs/architecture/domains/chat.md (chat verb dispatch).
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GritQL note: matches the member-access path `trpc.chat.<verb>.mutationOptions`
// regardless of what follows (the `(...)` call). `$verb` binds to whichever
// verb the AST captured; `$node` binds the whole span for the diagnostic.

language js

`trpc.chat.$verb.mutationOptions` as $node where {
  // This rule is "in-SURFACE" by name and intent: inline chat-verb mutations in a
  // SURFACE bypass §11 verb dispatch; in a hook (the sanctioned homes above) it's
  // exactly where it belongs. Fire only on surface files (biome-2.4 $filename guard)
  // so the verb-hook homes aren't false-flagged.
  $filename <: r".*/features/[^/]+/surfaces/.*",
  register_diagnostic(span=$node, message="trpc.chat.<verb>.mutationOptions outside the sanctioned verb-hook home — push the verb into features/chat/hooks/use-chat-verbs.ts (or use-chat-injection-verbs.ts / use-draft-chat-actions.ts / use-recent-chats-actions.ts depending on scope), and call the verb from this surface. See docs/architecture/domains/chat.md (chat verb dispatch).")
}
